                        "sense_id": "03170e00-8639-3669-b2f9-ec57e7b3807a",
                        "entry_id": "f4964775-75a3-31f7-915a-c570567379b3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Illuminated so as to dazzle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "60af57d9-464b-4a06-9a3a-33c5ca6b84af",
                                "sense_id": "03170e00-8639-3669-b2f9-ec57e7b3807a",
                                "text": "1832, John Wilson, Noctes Ambrosianæ No. LX, Blackwood’s Edinburgh Magazine, Volume 32, No. 190, February 1832, p. 281,\n[…] let [a poet] speak of a man-of-war in a style that shows he knows a frigate from a three-decker, a cutter from a schooner […] , and Neptune shall be to him Apollo, the Nereids the Muses, and every line shall be a line of light—all a-dazzle with appropriate words, surcharged with the imagery of the great deep."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b802a16e-8929-41be-a933-abc6f99db2af",
                                "sense_id": "03170e00-8639-3669-b2f9-ec57e7b3807a",
                                "text": "The dust rose up in thick clouds, thickened yet more by the sunlight held in them; for the dead air of the hollow was a-dazzle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2c1a821-6875-46cf-aaa4-a2330583b9c4",
                                "sense_id": "03170e00-8639-3669-b2f9-ec57e7b3807a",
                                "text": "It was an æsthetic education to live within those walls, to wander from room to room, from the Soanesque library to the Chinese drawing-room, adazzle with gilt pagodas and nodding mandarins […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a02e94a-6b37-4ff1-9c10-f6d9dc810f53",
                                "sense_id": "03170e00-8639-3669-b2f9-ec57e7b3807a",
                                "text": "By the time they entered Washington, it was dark and the lights of the city were all adazzle."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
